    {
      "id": "picard-iteration",
      "type": "ordinary-paragraph",
      "regions": [
        [
          12,
          95,
          1555,
          1040,
          1705
        ],
        [
          13,
          90,
          164,
          1040,
          447
        ]
      ],
      "english": "Then the fundamental theorem of calculus implies that $\\bm{y}$ is differentiable and satisfies \\eqref{eq:ode-initial-value-dynamics}, \\eqref{eq:ode-initial-value-data} (cf. the results on smoothness below). The solution of \\eqref{eq:ode-integral-equation} is obtained from an iterative procedure; i.e., we begin with an initial guess for the solution (usually the constant function $\\bm{y}_0$) and proceed to calculate\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:picard-iteration}\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\bm{y}_1(t)&=\\bm{y}_0+\\displaystyle\\int_{t_0}^t\\bm{F}(s,\\bm{y}_0)\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\\\\\n\\bm{y}_2(t)&=\\bm{y}_0+\\displaystyle\\int_{t_0}^t\\bm{F}(s,\\bm{y}_1(s))\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\\\\\n&\\ \\vdots\\\\\n\\bm{y}_{k+1}(t)&=\\bm{y}_0+\\displaystyle\\int_{t_0}^t\\bm{F}(s,\\bm{y}_k(s))\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\\\\\n&\\ \\vdots\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{equation}",
      "chinese": "于是微积分基本定理表明, $\\bm{y}$ 可微并满足 \\eqref{eq:ode-initial-value-dynamics}, \\eqref{eq:ode-initial-value-data} (参见下文关于光滑性的结果). 方程 \\eqref{eq:ode-integral-equation} 的解由迭代过程得到; 即从解的一个初始猜测 (通常取常值函数 $\\bm{y}_0$) 出发, 依次计算\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:picard-iteration}\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\bm{y}_1(t)&=\\bm{y}_0+\\displaystyle\\int_{t_0}^t\\bm{F}(s,\\bm{y}_0)\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\\\\\n\\bm{y}_2(t)&=\\bm{y}_0+\\displaystyle\\int_{t_0}^t\\bm{F}(s,\\bm{y}_1(s))\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\\\\\n&\\ \\vdots\\\\\n\\bm{y}_{k+1}(t)&=\\bm{y}_0+\\displaystyle\\int_{t_0}^t\\bm{F}(s,\\bm{y}_k(s))\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\\\\\n&\\ \\vdots\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{equation}",
      "label": null,
